{
  "_comment": "Retirement Bucket List. A long numbered list of short, concrete things to do in retirement, grouped under theme headings, each with a checkbox to tick when done. Variety is structural: the service samples a handful of themes per list from the bank below (always at least one from every group, the seller's focus weighted up), then gives every requested idea its own brief -- one of that theme's facets plus a cross-cutting flavour (free, at home, with a friend...) -- so a list cannot be twenty ways of saying 'travel'. Section titles are printed as written here, never by the model. An idea survives only as one short imperative action (see limits); repeats are caught on content words after qualifierWords are dropped, phrases and synonyms are folded, and genericWords (verbs like try/learn/visit, and the empty words of vague goals) are removed -- an idea left with nothing concrete is too vague to print. leadVerbs catch two ideas joined into one ('Bake bread and share it'). The same lists are mirrored in frontend/src/utils/studio/bucket-list/content.ts and checked by content-lists.test.ts.",
  "limits": {
    "rateLimitPerWindow": 10,
    "maxOutputTokens": 4096,
    "maxAttempts": 2,
    "batchItems": 36,
    "minSections": 5,
    "maxSections": 12,
    "itemsPerSection": 8,
    "minIdeaChars": 10,
    "maxIdeaChars": 52,
    "minIdeaWords": 2,
    "maxIdeaWords": 10,
    "maxConceptChars": 40
  },
  "locale": {
    "nativeLocales": ["en"],
    "nativeLine": "- Write in clear, warm, natural English that reads well in both British and American homes.",
    "otherLine": "- Write every idea in language locale '{locale}', natural for that language, keeping each idea a short action."
  },
